---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const timeline = [
  { year: '2018', text: 'I started producing electronic music out of curiosity.' },
  { year: '2020', text: 'First breakthrough with serious recognition in the progressive house community.' },
  { year: '2022', text: '"Magnets" was my first major collaboration, released on Glow Records.' },
  { year: '2023', text: '"Not What I Need" was released on Soulz Music Group.' },
  {
    year: '2024',
    text: 'I dropped two major tracks: "Embrace The Night" (Ensis Records) and "I\'m Broken" (Future House Cloud).',
  },
  {
    year: '2025',
    text: 'First official remix, "Morgen Untergehen" for Ann-Cathrin, followed by "Reminds Me Of You" on FeelQ Recordings.',
  },
  {
    year: '2026',
    text: 'Major release "Your Love (Is A Stranger)" on Hardwell\'s Revealed Recordings.',
  },
];

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'ProfilePage',
  mainEntity: {
    '@type': 'Person',
    name: 'Ozee',
    jobTitle: 'Electronic Music Producer',
    nationality: 'German',
    genre: ['Progressive House', 'Festival EDM'],
  },
};
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Learn about Ozee, a German progressive house and festival EDM producer active since 2018, with releases on labels including Glow Records, Soulz Music Group, Interplay Records, Stardust Records and more."
  image="/images/press/press-photo-1.jpeg"
  imageAlt="Ozee, progressive house and festival EDM producer, press photo"
  type="profile"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden pt-40 pb-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-2 items-center">
      <div>
        <p class="reveal text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-white/50 mb-4">About</p>
        <h1 class="reveal text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-6">My Story</h1>
        <p class="reveal text-white/70 leading-relaxed">
          I&rsquo;m an electronic music producer from Germany, shaping my sound since 2018.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal aspect-[4/5] rounded-3xl overflow-hidden border border-white/10">
        <img
          src="/images/press/press-photo-1.jpeg"
          alt="Portrait of Ozee, German progressive house and festival EDM producer"
          width="1204"
          height="1600"
          loading="eager"
          class="h-full w-full object-cover"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
    <h2 class="reveal text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Hey, I&rsquo;m Ozee.</h2>
    <div class="reveal space-y-6 text-white/80 leading-relaxed text-lg">
      <p>
        My journey started back in 2018 out of pure curiosity. I had no idea it would turn into
        the passion it is today, but along the way, artists like Martin Garrix, Alesso, and
        Hardwell got under my skin, and there was no turning back.
      </p>
      <p>
        From day one, my goal was never to just follow a formula. I love pulling influences from
        all different kinds of genres and throwing them into the mix. The result is a defined,
        unique sound that I&rsquo;m really proud of.
      </p>
      <p>
        Things really started moving in 2020, when I got my first real recognition in the
        progressive scene. That opened doors I didn&rsquo;t expect, and in 2022 I hit a big
        milestone with my first major collaboration, <a href="/releases/magnets/" class="underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-brand hover:text-brand-soft transition-colors">Magnets</a>,
        released on Glow Records. From there, things kept building: <a href="/releases/not-what-i-need/" class="underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-brand hover:text-brand-soft transition-colors">Not What I Need</a> dropped
        on Soulz Music Group in 2023, and 2024 brought two more releases close to my heart: <a href="/releases/embrace-the-night/" class="underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-brand hover:text-brand-soft transition-colors">Embrace The Night</a> on
        Ensis Records and <a href="/releases/im-broken/" class="underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-brand hover:text-brand-soft transition-colors">I'm Broken</a> on
        Future House Cloud.
      </p>
      <p>
        2025 has honestly been one of my favorite years yet. I got to produce my first official
        remix, <a href="/releases/morgen-untergehen/" class="underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-brand hover:text-brand-soft transition-colors">Morgen Untergehen</a>,
        for German singer-songwriter Ann-Cathrin, and joined FeelQ Recordings with <a href="/releases/reminds-me-of-you/" class="underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-brand hover:text-brand-soft transition-colors">Reminds Me Of You</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Then came 2026, and a dream came true. My collaboration <a href="/releases/your-love-is-a-stranger/" class="underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-brand hover:text-brand-soft transition-colors">Your Love (Is A Stranger)</a> got
        released on Hardwell&rsquo;s imprint, Revealed Radar. Growing up on his music, seeing my
        name on that label still feels a little surreal.
      </p>
      <p>
        With every track, I&rsquo;m just trying to get a little closer to the sound in my head.
        One that mixes emotion, energy, and a bit of experimentation. This is my journey, and
        I&rsquo;m excited for whatever comes next.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-y border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
      <h2 class="reveal text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mb-10">Timeline</h2>
      <ol class="reveal relative border-l border-white/15 space-y-10 pl-8">
        {
          timeline.map((item) => (
            <li>
              <span class="absolute -left-[7px] mt-1.5 h-3 w-3 rounded-full bg-brand" />
              <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-white/40 mb-1">{item.year}</p>
              <p class="text-white/80 leading-relaxed">{item.text}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 text-center">
    <h2 class="reveal text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mb-4">Sound &amp; Influences</h2>
    <p class="reveal text-white/70 leading-relaxed mb-8">
      I&rsquo;m rooted in the melodic progressive house genre that shaped artists like Martin
      Garrix, Alesso, and many more. But what defines my sound are genre-crossing influences,
      shaped through my own blend of emotion and energy.
    </p>
    <a
      href="/releases/"
      class="reveal btn-primary"
    >
      Explore my Releases
    </a>
  </section>
</Layout>
